      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_exact: position confirmed at this residue. validation_level surface_and_function -> function_only (paper reports surface: not_reported, function: yes). Paper (PMID 40489227): \"Single residue cysteine substitutions were prepared in the short splice variant of human NCKX2 cDNA ( AAF25811 ) with the c-myc tag (EQKLISEEDL) inserted between His83 and Gln84\". Audit note: Short splice variant (Q9UI40-2) differs from canonical only at 360-376, so His83/Gln84 numbering is unchanged. Function: K+-dependent Ca2+ transport (Fluo4) in HEK293 cells. This paper has no surface-display assay; the row's surface evidence comes from a different paper (PMC3576620), so surface_and_function is not supported by this PMID.] L4 explicitly names the junction as between His83 and Gln84 of the short splice variant of human NCKX2. Python confirms canonical residues 83=H and 84=Q, placing the site 31 residues from the TM1 C-boundary (52) and 56 residues from the TM2 N-boundary (139), well within the large extracellular loop EC1 (53\u2013138). The same paper (PMC3576620) confirms surface display of the FLAG-tagged construct (L2, L3), and L4 states transport activity was measured with the c-myc-tagged backbone, supporting surface_and_function classification. Full-length human NCKX2 short splice variant (AAF25811) with c-myc tag inserted between His83 and Gln84; construct used for cysteine-scanning mutagenesis and Na/Ca-K exchange transport activity assays in transfected cells. Canonical His83 and Gln84 confirmed by Python search: seq[82]='H', seq[83]='Q'. The short splice variant numbering matches canonical at this position exactly.",
