      "rationale": "L1 explicitly names the replaced residues as aa 90\u201397 (DLNDKIRD) in the NCKX2 construct. Python search finds DLNDKILD at canonical 89\u201396, consistent with a 1-residue numbering offset between the paper's isoform and the canonical sequence; the 7th residue (R vs L) is an isoform variant. The FLAG tag replaces canonical 89\u201396, so it is anchored after canonical residue 88 (L). L2 and L3 confirm the FLAG epitope is accessible at the extracellular surface by non-permeabilized immunolabeling, qualifying this as surface_only since transport function was not reported for this construct. Full-length NCKX2-FLAG construct created by replacing 8 residues (paper numbering aa 90\u201397, sequence DLNDKIRD) with the FLAG sequence (DYKDDDDK). Python locates the matching motif DLNDKI at canonical positions 89\u201394; the paper's numbering is 1-residue ahead of canonical (paper aa 90 = canonical 89), placing the replaced block at canonical 89\u201396 (DLNDKILD; the 7th residue differs R\u2192L between the paper's isoform and canonical, an isoform variant). The tag therefore follows canonical residue 88 (L); residue_after is canonical 89 (D) per schema convention. The site is 36 residues from TM1 end (52) and 51 residues from TM2 start (139), within EC1 (53\u2013138). Surface display confirmed by non-permeabilized anti-FLAG immunolabeling in hippocampal neurons (L2, L3).",
